The parametric `peak_summary` output no longer has the dominant-peak descriptors `peak_freq_dom`, `peak_power_dom` and `peak_bandwidth_dom`: the strongest peak over the fit range switches between rhythms from one spectrum to the next (alpha in one epoch, beta in the next), so its frequency mixes them, and it is NaN wherever no peak is fitted. A new `alpha_peak_present` (1 or 0) records whether a peak was fitted in the alpha band; `alpha_peak_freq` and `alpha_peak_power` stay NaN without one, never filled. Its recording mean is the share of epochs with an alpha peak. Parametric descriptors change and must be recomputed.
